            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0562" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War/9–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Alexander C. Kirk,
                        United States Political Adviser on the Staff of the Supreme Allied
                        Commander, Mediterranean Theater</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-07T12:00:00+02:00">September 7,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>312. My 295, September 4, midnight. General Wilson has now sent instructions to
                    Lieutenant Colonel Barnes that there is no objection to his meeting Von Lanz but
                    he is not to discuss terms of surrender. Purpose of such a meeting would be to
                    arrange evacuation of a senior German officer to AFHQ to receive surrender
                    terms.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
